{
  "title": "Taweez against Colitis",
  "data": "Those who suffer from colitis may write [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), [Surah al-Tawhid](A116), [Surah al-Falaq](A117) and [Surah al-Nas](A118) on a tablet or a sheet, and then add the following beneath them:\nاَعُوْذُ بِوَجْهِ اللّٰهِ الْعَظِيْمِ وَبِعِزَّتِهِ الَّتِىْ لَا تُرَامُ\nA'OODHU BIWAJHILLAAHIL A'ZEEMI WA BI-I'ZZATIHIL LATEE LAA TURAAM\nI seek refuge in the Face of Allah, the Great, and in His might, which cannot be attained,\nوَبِقُدْرَتِهِ الَّتِىْ لَا يَمْتَنِعُ مِنْهَا شَيْءٌ\nWA BIQUDRATIHIL LATEE LAA YAMTANI'U MINHAA SHAY'\nand in His power, from which nothing can hold back,\nمِنْ شَرِّ هٰذَا الْوَجَعِ وَمِنْ شَرِّ مَا فِيْهِ وَمِنْ شَرِّ مَا اَجِدُ مِنْهُ\nMIN SHARRI HAADHAL WAJA'I WA MIN SHARRI MAA FEEHI WA MIN SHARRI MAA AJIDU MINH\nfrom the evil of this pain, from the evil of what is in it, and from the evil of what I suffer from it.\nThe sheet may then be washed with rainwater, and the water drunk (1) at the beginning of the day, before eating anything, and (2) before going to sleep. This is a blessed and useful way.\nIt is narrated that a man complained to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) about colitis from which his brother suffered. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) instructed, “Tell your brother to drink a mixture of honey and hot water.” The next day, the man returned to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and said that the remedy had not helped. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said, “Allah is truthful, but your brother's belly lies. Go back, give him the same drink, and recite Surah al-Fatihah over it seven times.” When the man left, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said to Imam Ali (a.s.), “The brother of this man is a hypocrite; therefore, the drink did not help him.”"
}
